  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Near East South Asia Center / Office of the Secretary of Defense / Department of State Negev Forum Regional Security Working Group (RSWG) 01-23</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United States welcomes the opportunity to host Negev Forum members in Washington, DC for a series of discussions on regional security, cooperation opportunities, and information sharing. To open the program, the Near East South Asia Center, in support of the Department of Defense (DoD) Office of the Secretary of Defense (OSD) and the Department of State (DOS), will host a seminar in support of the Negev Forum Regional Security Working Group (RSWG). This seminar will provide a venue for participants to explore and identify areas of cooperation and disagreement, and develop proposals to promote progress. The seminar will allow the participants to hear different viewpoints and establish personal relationships. Participants will also constructively explore ways to enhance cooperation among their countries and build trust to advance strategic national interests. The program will include participants from Negev partner countries from the defense, security and diplomatic establishment.</narrative>
  </description>
